What is Sherlock?
Sherlock is an OSINT tool that searches for a username across 300+ social media platforms simultaneously.

---Installation
# Google Cloud Shell (git method -- recommended)
git clone https://github.com/sherlock-project/sherlock.git
cd sherlock
pip install tomli --break-system-packages
Access:
python3 -m sherlock_project username

# Kali Linux
sudo apt install sherlock -y
Access:
sherlock username



---All options:

# Basic search
python3 -m sherlock_project username

# Multiple usernames at once
python3 -m sherlock_project user1 user2 user3

# Save results to file
python3 -m sherlock_project username --output results.txt

# Search specific sites only
python3 -m sherlock_project username --site twitter instagram

# Set timeout (seconds)
python3 -m sherlock_project username --timeout 10

# Print all sites including not found
python3 -m sherlock_project username --print-all

# Print only found results (default)
python3 -m sherlock_project username --print-found

# Use proxy for anonymity
python3 -m sherlock_project username --proxy http://127.0.0.1:8080

# Open results in browser
python3 -m sherlock_project username --browse

# Export as CSV
python3 -m sherlock_project username --csv



---Important Notes

-Instagram and Facebook often block automated tools -- false negatives are common
-Always verify results manually by visiting the URL
-Many results can be false positives — check for profile photo, bio, and activity
-Use --print-all to see everything including non-matches
